    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d371">

                <pb facs="0521" n="509" sameAs="frus:frus1945v05/pg509"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to
                        the British Prime Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Churchill</hi>)<anchor n="22" xml:id="d371-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]<anchor n="23" xml:id="d371-f2"/>
                    </seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-03-11">11 March 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>714. Your 905. I have of course had very much in mind the considerations in
                    regard to Rumania and to the Polish question raised in your 905, March 8, and
                    share your concern over these developments. I am fully determined, as I know you
                    are, not to let the good decisions we reached at the Crimea slip through our
                    hands and will certainly do everything I can to hold Stalin to their honest
                    fulfillment. In regard to the Rumanian situation Averell has taken up and is
                    taking up again the whole question with Molotov invoking the Declaration on
                    Liberated Europe and has proposed tripartite discussions to carry out these
                    responsibilities. It is obvious that the Russians have installed a minority
                    government of their own choosing, but apart from the reasons you mentioned in
                    your message, Rumania <pb facs="0522" n="510" xml:id="pg510"/> is not a good
                    place for a test case. The Russians have been in undisputed control from the
                    beginning and with Rumania lying athwart the Russian lines of communications it
                    is moreover difficult to contest the plea of military necessity and security
                    which they are using to justify their action. We shall certainly do everything
                    we can, however, and of course will count on your support.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Roosevelt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
